{
  "verdict": "request_changes",
  "summary": "Candidate fails to cache missing SKU lookups, violating the caching requirement that each SKU must be read from the table at most once between updates.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "missing_sku_cache",
      "file": "candidate.py",
      "line_start": 11,
      "line_end": 14,
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "price() does not cache the result of a missing SKU lookup. Consecutive calls to price(\"missing\") will each invoke _read and increment reads, violating the contract that each SKU must be read at most once between two updates of that SKU.",
      "evidence": "```python\n# Catalog initialization\ncatalog = candidate.Catalog({\"a\": 1})\n# First missing SKU lookup\ncatalog.price(\"missing\")  # _read called, reads += 1\n# Second missing SKU lookup\ncatalog.price(\"missing\")  # _read called again, reads += 1\n# After these two calls, reads == 2, which violates the caching requirement.\n```"
    }
  ]
}
